title: "Creation Actualization Cosmology: A Position Paper for an Alternative Cosmological Research Programme"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Longmire
    given-names: James D.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1383-7698"
    email: jdlongmire@outlook.com
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-08"
url: "https://github.com/jdlongmire/creation-actualization-cosmology"
abstract: >
  Creation Actualization Cosmology proposes an alternative cosmological research
  programme founded on a different historical boundary condition: that the universe
  was discretely actualized into functional maturity during Creation Week and has
  operated under stable physical law since. It is offered as a Lakatosian research
  programme, not a quantitative cosmological model, and its own appraisal records it
  as unappraised with zero novel predictive content.
# Top-level `type` is constrained by CFF 1.2 to software/dataset; the repository
# carries Python traceability tooling, so `software` is retained. The scholarly
# object to cite is the position paper, given as preferred-citation below.
